5.4Worked example 1: generate pink in HSV (your question)
Given H = 0°, S = 0.5, V = 1.
V = C_max = 1, so R' = 1 (R = 255).
S = 1 − C_min/C_max = 0.5, so C_min = 0.5 (G' = B' = 0.5, i.e. 127.5).
H = 0° means red dominant with G' = B'.
(R,G,B) = (255,\ 128,\ 128) \approx \text{pink (light red)}
In RGB terms: keep R at 255 and raise G and B equally; pure red (255, 0, 0) has S = 1, and
lowering S adds white. Check: your RGB line for pink appears to read (255, 255, 255) with
